            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0000\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F001:F006\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposal accurately links C0001 as an exception qualifying baseline C0000, directly reflecting the statutory text of Subparagraph (B)(i) which provides that Subparagraph (A) shall not apply when the attorney general determines pre-filing notice is not feasible. The actor, action, logic, and scope text accurately reflect the source.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F001:F009\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposed summary introduces the separate mandatory duty from clause (ii) (represented by C0002) requiring simultaneous notice and a copy of the complaint upon filing. C0001 is rooted solely in clause (i) (F005:F006), which only governs the exemption from Subparagraph (A). Conflating the affirmative requirement of clause (ii) into C0001's summary is unsupported.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0002\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F001:F009\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The proposal incorrectly designates C0002 as the qualified claim in the qualifies field. F006 expressly exempts from Subparagraph (A) (C0000), not the simultaneous notice requirement in clause (ii) (C0002). In addition, the summary improperly blends the distinct obligation from clause (ii) into C0001.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
